{title: Hark! The Herald Angels Sing}
{artist: Charles Wesley / Felix Mendelssohn}
{genre: Christmas}
{flow: Opening}
{style: Carol}
{key: G}
{tempo: 104}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 126장}
{title_ko: 천사 찬송하기를}
{score: hark-the-herald-angels-sing.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Hark! the herald [D]angels sing
"[G]Glory to the [D]newborn [G]King
[G]Peace on earth and [D]mercy mild
[G]God and sinners [D]recon[G]ciled"
[C]Joyful, all ye [G]nations rise
[Am]Join the triumph [D]of the skies
[G]With the angelic [D]host pro[G]claim
"[C]Christ is [G]born in [D]Beth[G]lehem"
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Hark! the herald [D]angels sing
"[G]Glory to the [D]newborn [G]King"
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Christ, by highest [D]heaven adored
[G]Christ, the everlasting [D]Lord
[G]Late in time be[D]hold Him come
[G]Offspring of a [D]Vir[G]gin's womb
[C]Veiled in flesh the [G]Godhead see
[Am]Hail the incar[D]nate Deity
[G]Pleased as man with [D]men to dwell
[C]Jesus, our Em[G]manu[D]el[G]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Hail the heaven-born [D]Prince of Peace
[G]Hail the Sun of [D]Righteous[G]ness
[G]Light and life to [D]all He brings
[G]Risen with healing [D]in His [G]wings
[C]Mild He lays His [G]glory by
[Am]Born that man no [D]more may die
[G]Born to raise the [D]sons of earth
[C]Born to give them [G]second [D]birth[G]
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
